      "summaryMarkdown": "Passed. The final s00 mechanism records each measured leaf requested under view retention with its owning view and whether its style fixes its size in every parent. On the next frame it builds (`mark_view_dirty`, counted once) every view holding a non-text leaf that is not fixed or that Taffy measured to size it. Splice takes those views as gaps from `dirty_views`, so their ancestors are spliced, not built, and the layer and list-row checks honour the dirtiness. Text keeps its carry and replay paths, and fixed measured leaves keep their view reusable (`views_reused > 0`, 0 builds). With view retention off nothing is counted or changed. No frame-local closure crosses frames.\n\n**Accepted cost:** every view holding a non-fixed measured leaf is built on each drawn frame. This covers `uniform_list`/`list`/`VirtualList` with `Infer` and RayX's markup `inline_flow`, and matches d-retained-measured-leaves, which defers measurement replay to a later optimization driven by `views_built_for_measured_leaves`. Defaults (`ListSizingBehavior::Auto`, img, svg, text) are unaffected. The ML-1 group (9 tests) and the ML-2 oracle cover the cases. The sprint checks are fresh at revision 13.",
      "findingIds": [
