      ],
      "descriptionMarkdown": "Resolved. The style flag is replaced by recording, in the Taffy measure callback, every non-text leaf whose measurement can set its size. That is an axis of `known_dimensions.or(style size resolved against parent_size, with the aspect ratio applied)` left `None`; ContentSize mode uses `known_dimensions` alone, mirroring taffy 0.14 `compute_leaf_layout`. This catches percentages of an indefinite parent and the flex automatic-minimum probe, and keeps leaves of definite size reusable. New cases `PercentOfAutoParent` and `DefiniteFlexChild`. The transition case the new mechanism cannot see is filed as lk-s00-F4.",
      "boundaryId": "s00-measured-leaves"
    },
    {
      "id": "lk-s00-F2",
      "criterionIds": [
        "ML-2"
      ],
      "severity": "minor",
      "status": "resolved",
      "regressionRefs": [
        {
          "repositoryId": "gpux",
          "path": "crates/gpui/tests/retained_measured_leaves.rs"
        }
      ],
      "descriptionMarkdown": "Resolved. The counter now counts once per view, at draw start, when `Window::draw` marks a measuring view dirty that was not already dirty. It no longer counts refusals inside `keep_retained_nodes`, so the double count through `reuse_kept_layout` and the layer-content count are gone. The tests bound the count exactly per mode (0 without view retention, 0 in the definite case with `views_reused > 0`), with stats reset after `set_fast_mode`.",
      "boundaryId": "s00-measured-leaves"
    },
    {
      "id": "lk-s00-F3",
      "criterionIds": [
        "ML-2"
      ],
      "severity": "minor",
      "status": "resolved",
      "regressionRefs": [
        {
          "repositoryId": "gpux",
          "path": "crates/gpui/tests/retained_measured_leaves.rs"
        }
      ],
      "descriptionMarkdown": "Resolved. The measuring view is `mark_view_dirty`'d, which dirties its ancestors exactly as a notify does. With splice on, `splice_layout` takes dirty nested views from `dirty_views` as gaps (splice.rs:399), and the view is not in `notified`, so its ancestors are spliced, not built. Without splice, they cost what a notify of that view costs. The dirtying happens before `invalidator.set_dirty(false)`, so it schedules no extra frames.",
      "boundaryId": "s00-measured-leaves"
    },
    {
      "id": "lk-s00-F4",
      "criterionIds": [
        "ML-1"
      ],
      "severity": "major",
      "status": "resolved",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "Resolved. `Window::note_measured_owner` records every measured leaf requested under view retention with `fast::layout::measured_size_is_fixed(style)`. That means an absolute width and height, plus an absolute `min_size` on both axes or overflow Hidden/Scroll on both axes. Before clear, the owners of every non-text leaf that is not fixed, or that Taffy measured to size it, are built on the next frame, so a leaf that can become indefinite is never kept. Checked against taffy 0.14: a fixed leaf's size never comes from its measurement. Its InherentSize probes resolve the style size (leaf.rs:61, 147). The flex base size takes the definite main size. The automatic minimum is skipped by an absolute min size or a non-visible overflow (flexbox.rs:1037). The intrinsic-main path (flexbox.rs:1405) and the hypothetical cross size (flexbox.rs:1819) use the preferred size, and the baseline and absolute-child ContentSize calls pass both dimensions. The stated residual (a fixed leaf probed while kept) therefore has no reachable size effect. Regression: `a_kept_leaf_keeps_its_size_when_its_parent_becomes_flex` (red on the previous source) and `a_kept_leaf_keeps_its_size_when_its_parent_loses_its_height`.",
      "regressionRefs": [
        {
          "repositoryId": "gpux",
          "path": "crates/gpui/tests/retained_measured_leaves.rs"
        }
      ],
      "boundaryId": "s00-measured-leaves"
    }
  ],
